1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,503
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:07,382
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,593
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,804
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:19,853
[Samir, in English] <i>The man who broke</i>
<i>into the ambassador's office.</i>

7
00:00:19,936 --> 00:00:21,146
[in English] <i>He might be here too.</i>

8
00:00:21,229 --> 00:00:22,230
[gunshots]

9
00:00:22,313 --> 00:00:23,231
[screaming and panicking]

10
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:24,524
Son of a thread.

11
00:00:24,607 --> 00:00:26,317
[Mercado on phone]
<i>Lily Santiago is the head</i>

12
00:00:26,401 --> 00:00:28,611
<i>of the IT of the embassy.</i>

13
00:00:28,695 --> 00:00:30,030
[in English] Where is she?

14
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:30,947
[grunts]

15
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:32,365
[grunts]

16
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:34,325
PREVIOUSLY

17
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:35,243
[sobbing]

18
00:00:35,326 --> 00:00:36,161
[Samir, in English] <i>Where is the girl?</i>

19
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,788
[wails]

20
00:00:38,872 --> 00:00:40,457
[armed man] Sir, they're here, sir!

21
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,083
[on phone] <i>We're about to catch them, sir!</i>

22
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,918
[grunts and groans]

23
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:45,128
[grunting]

24
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:46,045
[gunshots]

25
00:00:48,047 --> 00:00:50,508
[Samir, in English]
<i>Before I do something to you,</i>

26
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:53,261
<i>I want to see your face.</i>

27
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:56,056
[Charmi] <i>Friend, maybe you should</i>
<i>focus on Ibyang first.</i>

28
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:57,140
[Olga] <i>Maybe you're right.</i>

29
00:00:57,223 --> 00:01:00,351
The child hasn't done anything wrong
for me to treat her that way.

30
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:02,020
Even my own child.

31
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:04,606
[in English] This has to stop!
You're a monster!

32
00:01:04,689 --> 00:01:08,109
This is the first time
I've had such a beautiful doll.

33
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:09,694
[Olga] <i>You're a meddler!</i>

34
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:11,362
Did I tell you to take this?!

35
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:12,989
[Red, in English] I'm sure
you know that seal, right?

36
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:14,407
[in English] He is the mastermind!

37
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:15,450
[in English] What's going on here?

38
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:20,038
[in English] Are you involved
in human trafficking?

39
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:21,790
[in English] Audrey, let me explain.

40
00:01:21,873 --> 00:01:23,166
[in English] I trusted you!

41
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:27,128
[Audrey] <i>I chose you over Atoy!</i>
<i>But you were deceiving me!</i>

42
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:29,798
Brother! Psst, hey!

43
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:31,591
Brother! [sobs]

44
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:36,012
[in English] I'm sorry.

45
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:38,431
I didn't tell you everything.

46
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:42,227
I stepped down from the business

47
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:44,646
and let Red take over.

48
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:47,148
But you're still part of it!

49
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:51,027
[in English] That doesn't make you
any less guilty, Dad!

50
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:56,241
And you even used Bahay Kayakap
as a front to do evil!

51
00:01:56,950 --> 00:02:00,787
Don't you feel any shame
for what you've been doing?

52
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:02,247
- Audrey, I am not going to justify--
- You

53
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:06,626
rescue women only to harm them further?

54
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:10,713
Do you really have no conscience?!

55
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:13,174
[dark sinister music playing]

56
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:16,553
[in English] Like I said,
I'm not going to justify anything,

57
00:02:17,887 --> 00:02:20,265
and I know you don't want
to be a part of this.

58
00:02:21,141 --> 00:02:22,809
But this…

59
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:26,146
- This has become our family's business.
- [scoffs]

60
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:32,735
Even if it hurts me…

61
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:37,240
[in English] But you can leave this house,
leave the country.

62
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:38,283
[pensive music playing]

63
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:40,160
[in English] Go wherever you want.

64
00:02:41,202 --> 00:02:43,913
[in English] Take Janine with you
and start anew.

65
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:52,130
Don't put this family in danger.

66
00:02:52,964 --> 00:02:55,967
[in English] Please, my child. Please?

67
00:02:56,759 --> 00:02:58,887
[in English] So, you want me to look away?

68
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:01,639
[in English] To turn a blind eye?

69
00:03:03,516 --> 00:03:05,184
[in English] All I'm asking you

70
00:03:06,102 --> 00:03:07,979
is to consider your family.

71
00:03:08,646 --> 00:03:10,315
We're not perfect,

72
00:03:11,649 --> 00:03:13,693
but I hope you choose us.

73
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:19,032
[in English] Just the way your mother
chose our family over everything.

74
00:03:21,075 --> 00:03:22,535
Your mother knew all of this.

75
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,038
[in English] She never agreed.

76
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:29,709
But family weighed more for her.

77
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:36,007
[Audrey, in English] Dad?
Dad, what's happening?

78
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:38,218
- [in English] Dad, sit, sit, sit.
- [groans]

79
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:43,223
[pensive music playing]

80
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:44,432
[Audrey gasps]

81
00:03:44,515 --> 00:03:46,059
[Audrey] You need to be taken
to the hospital.

82
00:03:46,142 --> 00:03:47,435
Gavin!

83
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:49,604
Gavin, take Dad to the hospital!

84
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:50,772
[Dmitri] Audrey.

85
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:55,568
[in English] Please, promise me.

86
00:03:56,527 --> 00:03:59,072
You won't do anything
with what you've learned.

87
00:03:59,822 --> 00:04:01,199
[in English] Please, child.

88
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:06,704
I'm just a little stressed,
that's why my wound opened.

89
00:04:07,413 --> 00:04:10,875
[in English] Please? Please, my child.

90
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:12,585
Gavin!

91
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:14,754
- [Audrey] Gavin!
- Auntie?

92
00:04:14,837 --> 00:04:16,965
- Auntie!
- Take Dad to the hospital!

93
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:18,841
- His wound is bleeding.
- Grandpa.

94
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:21,803
- I'll follow.
- Okay, Auntie.

95
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:23,680
Come on, Grandpa.

96
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:28,851
[sinister music playing]

97
00:04:42,865 --> 00:04:45,076
If it's Audrey,
Dad is very easy to persuade.

98
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:46,286
[in English] That's a fact.

99
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:47,203
‪[scoffs]

100
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:52,375
[mysterious music playing]

101
00:04:52,458 --> 00:04:54,085
[in English] Gavin just messaged again.

102
00:04:54,168 --> 00:04:56,754
We really need to go to the hospital.

103
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:59,882
[in English] We have to see your dad,
especially you.

104
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:02,802
[suspicious music playing]

105
00:05:02,885 --> 00:05:03,803
No.

106
00:05:04,554 --> 00:05:05,638
We'll stay here.

107
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:07,974
[in English] Why?

108
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:13,813
[music fades]

109
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:16,566
[suave theme music playing]

110
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:36,461
[music swells]

111
00:05:36,544 --> 00:05:38,755
[electronic blipping]

112
00:05:40,798 --> 00:05:42,341
[grunts]

113
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:45,511
[pants and sobs]

114
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:48,097
[Lily, in English] I don't know
where it is!

115
00:05:48,931 --> 00:05:50,224
[in English] And I don't know who…

116
00:05:50,308 --> 00:05:51,851
[in English] I don't know
who he is, I told you.

117
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:54,353
[in English] I've never--
I've never met him in my entire life!

118
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:55,855
[in English] You are lying!

119
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:59,108
[in English] I am not lying. [sobs]

120
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:02,111
[in English] Then why did he try
to protect you? Hmm?

121
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:04,572
[Samir, in English] Why did he try
to save you?

122
00:06:04,655 --> 00:06:05,490
‪[Lily sobs]

123
00:06:05,573 --> 00:06:08,493
[in English] It's because you two
are working together!

124
00:06:08,576 --> 00:06:10,912
[tense music playing]

125
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:13,956
Huh?

126
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:20,254
[Lily pants]

127
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:24,133
[in English] We are not working together.

128
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:27,095
[suspicious music playing]

129
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:28,888
[in English] Well, well, well.

130
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:32,600
[in English] Look who decided
to join the party.

131
00:06:33,351 --> 00:06:34,894
[in English] Good morning.

132
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:43,820
[in English] You are ready
to talk now, yes?

133
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:50,243
[in English] Let's make this simple.

134
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:51,994
[in English] Yes?

135
00:06:54,163 --> 00:06:56,290
[in English] I will ask you a question.

136
00:06:57,166 --> 00:06:59,919
[in English] If you answer, you can go.

137
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:01,629
[suspicious music playing]

138
00:07:01,712 --> 00:07:02,922
[Samir, in English] But

139
00:07:03,923 --> 00:07:05,633
if you don't…

140
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:08,678
you will not go.

141
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:11,848
[in English] Yes?

142
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:16,352
[in English] Where is the laptop?

143
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:26,863
Mmm.

144
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:31,284
[in English] Okay.
You don't want to talk to me.

145
00:07:37,373 --> 00:07:38,583
[in English] I see.

146
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:44,839
- [grunts]
- [in English] No, no, no, no, no!

147
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:45,923
- [grunts]
- [Lily, in English] No!

148
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:47,341
[Lily sobs]

149
00:07:47,425 --> 00:07:48,634
[Atoy coughs]

150
00:07:48,718 --> 00:07:50,428
[tense music playing]

151
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:54,265
[in English] So,
if you don't want to talk…

152
00:07:56,642 --> 00:07:58,728
maybe we can play a little game.

153
00:07:58,811 --> 00:07:59,937
- [in English] Yes?
- [in English] Yes!

154
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:03,941
[in English] You like games?

155
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,359
[groans]

156
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:07,361
[in English] Yes.

157
00:08:07,445 --> 00:08:09,238
- [Samir, in English] Perfect.
- [groans]

158
00:08:12,617 --> 00:08:15,161
[sobs]

159
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:19,081
[ominous music playing]

160
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:20,500
[dagger clatters]

161
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:25,421
[in English] Cut him.

162
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:31,511
[in English] Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no!

163
00:08:31,594 --> 00:08:32,929
[Lily] Please! Don't, don't, don't, don't.

164
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:34,096
Brother, don't!

165
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:35,223
[grunts]

166
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:51,572
[in English] If you do not
want to make this simple,

167
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:56,118
I will make it very, very hard for you.

168
00:08:56,202 --> 00:09:00,206
[pensive music playing]

169
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,041
[grunts]

170
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:04,877
[in English] You tell me now.

171
00:09:04,961 --> 00:09:07,463
[in English] Who are you working for?

172
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:10,758
[in English] And where is my briefcase?

173
00:09:11,842 --> 00:09:15,596
[heavy music playing]

174
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:16,722
[in English] Okay.

175
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:20,935
[in English] I will, I will…
I will tell you.

176
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:23,396
[in English] The briefcase is…

177
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:26,691
[in English] Briefcase is…

178
00:09:28,025 --> 00:09:30,069
- in my…
- [in English] In your?

179
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:31,320
[in English] In my nose.

180
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:32,822
[tense music playing]

181
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:33,864
[in English] No!

182
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:38,202
Stop, please!

183
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:39,870
[Lily sobs] No.

184
00:09:40,788 --> 00:09:43,541
[sobbing] No, please!

185
00:09:43,624 --> 00:09:46,836
[Samir, in English]
Where is my briefcase?!

186
00:09:46,919 --> 00:09:49,839
[Samir, in English] Three, two, one!

187
00:09:49,922 --> 00:09:50,756
- [grunts]
- [Lily shrieks]

188
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:51,799
[in English] No!

189
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:52,592
[Lily, in English] Please, stop it!

190
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:54,135
[in English] Who are you working for?!

191
00:09:54,218 --> 00:09:55,261
[panting]

192
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:58,222
[in English] Three, two, one!

193
00:09:58,306 --> 00:09:59,890
- [groans]
- [Lily wails, in English] No!

194
00:09:59,974 --> 00:10:02,602
[in English] Tell me
where my briefcase is.

195
00:10:02,685 --> 00:10:03,894
[in English] Do you want to talk?

196
00:10:03,978 --> 00:10:07,523
[in English] Yes. It is
in your, in your… in your pocket!

197
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:08,858
- [in English] In your left pocket.
- [growls]

198
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:10,151
[grunts]

199
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:11,777
[groaning and growling]

200
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:14,697
- [grunts]
- [Lily wailing]

201
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:17,033
[groans and wails, in English] No!

202
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:19,827
- [Samir groans]
- [grunts]

203
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:22,204
[heavy pained breathing]

204
00:10:22,288 --> 00:10:24,915
- [Lily, in English] No, no. Please, no!
- [grunts]

205
00:10:24,999 --> 00:10:26,334
- [groans]
- [Lily wailing]

206
00:10:27,209 --> 00:10:31,339
[ominous music playing]

207
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:36,052
[in English] Are you ready to tell me now
where my laptop is?

208
00:10:38,846 --> 00:10:40,264
[in English] Nope? Okay.

209
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:42,558
[Lily, in English] No! No!

210
00:10:43,559 --> 00:10:46,437
- [Samir, in English] Yes.
- [in English] Are you… Are you tired?

211
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:49,940
[in English] You, you whip
so, so, so weak!

212
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,692
[cackles]

213
00:10:54,153 --> 00:10:56,822
[speaking in Russian]
I'll beat the living hell…

214
00:10:56,906 --> 00:11:00,868
[indistinct]

215
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:02,411
[speaking in Russian] …you bastard!

216
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:09,251
[speaking in Visayan]
Please, stop it already!

217
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:15,424
[wailing, indistinct]

218
00:11:18,594 --> 00:11:19,678
[coughs]

219
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:20,971
[grunts]

220
00:11:26,644 --> 00:11:30,314
[sobbing]

221
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:45,913
[music fades]

222
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,299
Hey, Ibyang!

223
00:11:59,301 --> 00:12:00,219
[Charmi] Ibyang!

224
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:02,263
[melancholic music playing]

225
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:04,181
What are you doing there?

226
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:07,309
Why is the pretty child crying?

227
00:12:07,893 --> 00:12:08,978
Hey.

228
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:13,357
Mama scolded me.

229
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:18,112
[sobs] Then she said I'm not her child.

230
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:22,700
What happened?

231
00:12:22,783 --> 00:12:25,244
Why did Mama Olga scold you?

232
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:31,125
Because I broke the doll
that I thought was a gift for me.

233
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:34,086
Hmm, the doll.

234
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:39,341
You know, Ibyang?

235
00:12:40,259 --> 00:12:43,721
That's just how Mama Olga is.
She's sometimes strict.

236
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:47,850
You know, sometimes when we fight,
we have misunderstandings.

237
00:12:47,933 --> 00:12:50,478
She even tells me
we're not friends anymore.

238
00:12:50,561 --> 00:12:52,229
But that's not true,

239
00:12:52,313 --> 00:12:54,565
because we're friends no matter what.

240
00:12:54,648 --> 00:12:57,234
[in English] Through thick and thin,
through sickness and in health.

241
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:58,903
[in English] So help me, God.

242
00:12:58,986 --> 00:12:59,820
‪[quirky sting]

243
00:13:01,655 --> 00:13:02,865
Well…

244
00:13:02,948 --> 00:13:06,285
That's just how your Mama Olga is.
She's sometimes strict.

245
00:13:06,368 --> 00:13:08,871
But even if she's stern sometimes,

246
00:13:08,954 --> 00:13:11,373
she's kind most of the time.

247
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:14,126
She's crazy, but very kind.

248
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:19,298
That's why I'm sure she didn't mean
to say you're not her child.

249
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:23,844
You are her child. You are her daughter.

250
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:27,640
Come on, oh! Look, you even look alike!

251
00:13:27,723 --> 00:13:29,975
[Charmi chuckles, in English] Olga Junior!

252
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:36,273
[melodramatic music playing]

253
00:13:37,274 --> 00:13:38,400
Mmm.

254
00:13:39,109 --> 00:13:42,279
Just be patient with Mama Olga,
okay, child.

255
00:13:43,656 --> 00:13:45,449
Go upstairs now.

256
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:48,827
She might get angry if she can't find you.

257
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:50,287
Go on. Go now.

258
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:52,706
Stop crying. Stop crying, stop crying.

259
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:53,958
Smile now, okay?

260
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:55,960
Smile.

261
00:14:03,842 --> 00:14:04,843
[softly, in English] Pajamas.

262
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,519
[in English] Mommy.

263
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:16,480
Are we leaving?

264
00:14:23,362 --> 00:14:24,530
[in English] Yes, child.

265
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:29,201
Where are we going?

266
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:32,705
To the States.

267
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,333
To America?

268
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:38,210
Yay!

269
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:40,671
I'll finally see snow!

270
00:14:40,754 --> 00:14:42,548
Child, my child, my child. Wait, wait.

271
00:14:43,132 --> 00:14:44,383
Listen first.

272
00:14:45,342 --> 00:14:48,804
I'm sorry if this trip is sudden.

273
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:52,683
But we need to visit
your Daddy Atoy first.

274
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:56,186
- [in English] Okay?
- Okay.

275
00:14:57,354 --> 00:14:59,690
Go get dressed now.

276
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:05,738
[tense music playing]

277
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:37,853
[melancholic music playing]

278
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:41,148
[in English] Sorry, Mama.

279
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:45,653
[sobs] Because of me,

280
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:47,821
the doll was broken.

281
00:15:50,407 --> 00:15:54,870
[sobs] It won't happen again. Promise.

282
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:00,876
[in English] I love you, Mama.

283
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:35,369
[in English] Let's go, child.

284
00:16:36,286 --> 00:16:37,579
Ma'am, are you leaving?

285
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:38,998
Yes. Please open the gate.

286
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:40,124
Ah. Okay, ma'am.

287
00:16:40,207 --> 00:16:43,836
I'm so excited, Mommy!
It's my dream to go to America!

288
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:46,755
[tense music playing]

289
00:16:46,839 --> 00:16:47,965
- Get in, child.
- [Janine, in English] Okay.

290
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,325
[in English] Let me help you
with your seatbelt, dear.

291
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:21,999
[Janine, in English] Mommy, Mommy.

292
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:24,543
Are you in a hurry?

293
00:17:26,628 --> 00:17:27,755
No one leaves.

294
00:17:29,506 --> 00:17:30,758
[Red] Try to start that.

295
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:33,052
Try it.

296
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:43,270
[line ringing]

297
00:17:43,353 --> 00:17:45,189
What happened to you, Padua?

298
00:17:45,773 --> 00:17:48,275
[automated voice, in English]
<i>Please try your call later.</i>

299
00:17:48,358 --> 00:17:49,234
[keyboard clicks]

300
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:51,445
<i>My husband is now in the hospital.</i>

301
00:17:51,528 --> 00:17:56,450
[in English] <i>I know as a mayor, my husband</i>
<i>has several death threats.</i>

302
00:17:56,533 --> 00:18:00,454
<i>Whoever entered and caused trouble</i>
<i>in my home,</i>

303
00:18:00,537 --> 00:18:05,626
<i>we will make sure you are punished.</i>

304
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:11,590
[line ringing]

305
00:18:11,673 --> 00:18:13,675
[in English] I need you
to report to me in person.

306
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:16,345
- [in English] Padua is compromised.
- [rousing music playing]

307
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:18,305
- Stop it!
- Aunt Martina!

308
00:18:18,388 --> 00:18:19,640
[in English] Martina, stop!

309
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:20,682
- [in English] Stop!
- [in English] Mommy!

310
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:21,850
You're hurting her!

311
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:23,769
Stop it! Let her go!

312
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,563
- You're too noisy.
- Red!

313
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:28,398
- [in English] Mommy, Mommy!
- Please! Put down your gun!

314
00:18:28,482 --> 00:18:30,400
The child is scared!

315
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:33,821
Martina is hurting her! Stop it! Stop!

316
00:18:33,904 --> 00:18:35,656
[gasps, in English] Mommy.

317
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:37,658
Sir Red, I'm sorry.

318
00:18:37,741 --> 00:18:40,202
I heard Ma'am Janine
and Ma'am Audrey shouting.

319
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:42,663
- I thought--
- What did you think, huh?

320
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:45,749
No one leaves this house.

321
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:49,169
Lock the gate.

322
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:52,965
Don't tell anyone.
Don't say you saw anything.

323
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:55,717
If you want to go home to your family.

324
00:18:56,426 --> 00:18:57,511
Clear?

325
00:18:58,303 --> 00:18:59,429
Yes.

326
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:01,557
- Go now.
- Okay.

327
00:19:05,102 --> 00:19:07,104
Where are you going?

328
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:08,397
To the hospital.

329
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:10,566
We're going to see Dad at the hospital.

330
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:13,861
In case you didn't know,
his wound got worse.

331
00:19:14,486 --> 00:19:16,780
Hospital, but you're bringing
your luggage?

332
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:18,157
What's that, a vacation?

333
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:22,828
You even brought this evidence
that could ruin your family.

334
00:19:23,829 --> 00:19:25,289
[in English] No… No, Red.

335
00:19:25,372 --> 00:19:28,167
I promised Dad I wouldn't speak out.

336
00:19:31,044 --> 00:19:32,462
[in English] Please, just let us go.

337
00:19:35,132 --> 00:19:36,550
[grunts and groans]

338
00:19:36,633 --> 00:19:37,676
[in English] Mommy?

339
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:39,344
[screams]

340
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,221
- [in English] Mommy! Mommy!
- [Red] Take them to my old room!

341
00:19:41,305 --> 00:19:42,514
[in English] Mommy!

342
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:48,270
Make sure you dispose of Audrey's car.

343
00:19:53,108 --> 00:19:55,027
Let me go! Mommy!

344
00:19:55,110 --> 00:19:57,654
[bawling]

345
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,781
[in English] Mommy! Mommy!

346
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,742
[wails]

347
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:04,828
Mommy! Please, wake up!

348
00:20:05,662 --> 00:20:08,415
Mommy! Why did you bring me
and my mommy here?!

349
00:20:08,498 --> 00:20:10,000
You're all cruel!

350
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:11,335
[squeals]

351
00:20:11,418 --> 00:20:12,461
Be quiet.

352
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:14,296
And stop with your "Mommy, Mommy"!

353
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:16,173
[whimpering]

354
00:20:17,507 --> 00:20:19,468
This is just their temporary cell.

355
00:20:20,093 --> 00:20:22,429
They can't stay here long.
Dad might come back.

356
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:24,640
[in English] So,
what's your plan with them?

357
00:20:26,558 --> 00:20:27,976
There are many things we can do with them.

358
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:31,897
Especially with the child.
We can use her to make money.

359
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:36,735
You, get a gag and ropes for these two.

360
00:20:36,818 --> 00:20:40,030
And no one should know they're here. Okay?

361
00:20:40,948 --> 00:20:43,283
[tense music playing]

362
00:20:54,544 --> 00:20:57,339
[sobs]

363
00:20:57,422 --> 00:21:00,300
[music fades]

364
00:21:01,009 --> 00:21:03,053
[Charmi clears throat]

365
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:05,347
Friend?

366
00:21:08,141 --> 00:21:09,184
Friend!

367
00:21:19,653 --> 00:21:20,862
Ibyang?

368
00:21:21,488 --> 00:21:22,823
Ibyang, wake up.

369
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:28,078
Wake up, child. Wake up.

370
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:44,886
[Charmi] Oh? Have you reconciled
with Mama Olga?

371
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:46,346
Where's your mama?

372
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:49,558
Friend! Olga!

373
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:51,435
Frie…

374
00:21:52,185 --> 00:21:54,438
Mama slept here.

375
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:57,357
I slept beside her.

376
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:04,906
Maybe she's still angry with me.

377
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:06,491
[melancholic music playing]

378
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:09,995
[clears throat]

379
00:22:10,078 --> 00:22:12,080
Just let your Mama Olga be.

380
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:15,042
She just went out. She'll come back.

381
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:17,627
Who is Sammy?

382
00:22:19,713 --> 00:22:24,843
Because Mama mentioned her name
last night while crying.

383
00:22:27,179 --> 00:22:29,222
Ah. [sighs]

384
00:22:29,306 --> 00:22:32,434
Ibyang, because it's not really…

385
00:22:34,144 --> 00:22:37,022
It's not really for me to tell.

386
00:22:37,606 --> 00:22:42,527
But Mama might not tell me herself.

387
00:22:43,153 --> 00:22:46,156
I just want to understand her.

388
00:22:48,283 --> 00:22:50,494
Does Mama have another child?

389
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:53,997
- Uh…
- Is it Sammy?

390
00:22:55,582 --> 00:22:57,250
Where is she?

391
00:22:57,918 --> 00:22:58,960
Um…

392
00:23:00,003 --> 00:23:01,171
[sighs]

393
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:02,255
[sighs]

394
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:09,054
Child, Sammy is Mama Olga's child
who died.

395
00:23:09,846 --> 00:23:12,724
So, she's your sibling.

396
00:23:16,561 --> 00:23:21,108
Why didn't Mama tell me
that I had a sibling?

397
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:31,368
Let's just try to understand Mama Olga.

398
00:23:31,451 --> 00:23:34,579
Because it's painful for her.

399
00:23:34,663 --> 00:23:36,164
That's why she's sad.

400
00:23:38,708 --> 00:23:40,335
Can you do that?

401
00:23:51,888 --> 00:23:54,975
[music fades]

402
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:04,442
[ominous music playing]

403
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:20,083
[gasping]

404
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:22,544
[tense sinister music playing]

405
00:24:22,627 --> 00:24:23,461
‪[groans]

406
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:27,465
[muttering and sobbing]

407
00:24:30,719 --> 00:24:31,887
[Audrey] My child.

408
00:24:32,429 --> 00:24:38,476
[muttering and sobbing]

409
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:42,814
‪My child.

410
00:24:48,862 --> 00:24:49,905
‪[whimpers]

411
00:24:50,447 --> 00:24:51,281
‪[Audrey] No!

412
00:24:55,869 --> 00:24:57,537
[Mongki, in English]
Good morning, Ms. Audrey.

413
00:24:57,621 --> 00:25:01,708
[wailing and muttering]

414
00:25:04,002 --> 00:25:06,880
- [Mongki] Good night again.
- [wailing and muttering]

415
00:25:06,963 --> 00:25:09,966
[Mongki] Sleep soundly there.
Just like your baby girl.

416
00:25:10,634 --> 00:25:12,177
[music fades]

417
00:25:12,260 --> 00:25:16,681
[wailing and muttering]

418
00:25:31,238 --> 00:25:34,115
[tense music playing]

419
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:38,245
[electronic blipping]

420
00:25:38,328 --> 00:25:41,957
[intense music playing]

421
00:25:44,542 --> 00:25:46,503
Can you take the child from me?

422
00:25:46,586 --> 00:25:47,504
[Olga on the phone] <i>I quit.</i>

423
00:25:47,587 --> 00:25:49,464
I'm already annoyed with her.

424
00:25:49,547 --> 00:25:50,882
- [Olga] <i>She's too meddlesome.</i>
- [wailing]

425
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:52,425
- [wailing]
- [shrieks]

426
00:25:52,509 --> 00:25:54,552
UP NEXT

427
00:25:55,136 --> 00:25:56,137
[in English] Mama!

428
00:25:56,221 --> 00:25:57,430
[grunts] Help us!

429
00:25:57,514 --> 00:25:58,723
- [Emerson coughs]
- [screaming and panicking]

430
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:02,185
Oh, no!
Emerson's Tailoring Shop is burning!

431
00:26:02,269 --> 00:26:04,104
- [grunts]
- Emerson!

432
00:26:04,187 --> 00:26:05,105
Ouch!

433
00:26:05,188 --> 00:26:06,064
[screaming and panicking]

434
00:26:06,147 --> 00:26:07,399
[firetruck siren wailing]

435
00:26:11,194 --> 00:26:14,823
[screaming and panicking]

436
00:26:16,741 --> 00:26:18,076
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

437
00:26:18,159 --> 00:26:20,412
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

438
00:26:20,495 --> 00:26:23,665
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

439
00:26:23,748 --> 00:26:25,500
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

440
00:26:25,583 --> 00:26:27,002
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
